  "description": "The missing super-pairwise binding magnitude cannot be VALIDATED from AME light nuclei at any order: over all 27 mirror-convention combinations every cumulant b3..b7 is determined to under one significant digit (best b6, 0.865), and b4/b3 -- the quantity this arc scores candidates against -- to 0.030 digits (93.3% band, a factor of 2.4). The one convention-invariant feature, the (+,+,-,+,-) sign pattern, is mostly generic -- 2 of 5 arbitrary peaked functions reproduce it -- and its whole discriminating content is that w is CONVEX on the rise to the peak, a sign condition not a magnitude. Scope-(a) and about the DATA, not the framework: it refutes no mechanism, and says AME light-nucleus binding is the wrong observable to test one against.",
